multichoice[20]{tags,text,exhibit,correct,w1,w2,w3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Which statement about the transport and message format of gNMI is correct?",,"gNMI runs over gRPC on HTTP/2 and exchanges protobuf messages","gNMI runs over SSH and exchanges XML RPCs","gNMI runs over HTTPS and exchanges resource-style JSON requests","gNMI runs over UDP and exchanges SNMP PDUs","gNMI is a gRPC service, so its requests and responses are protobuf messages carried over HTTP/2. XML over SSH describes NETCONF, and resource-style HTTPS requests describe RESTCONF.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","What does a filter inside an ACI contract subject define?",,"The protocols and ports that the subject matches, such as TCP port 443","Which tenant owns the contract","Which bridge domain the provider EPG uses","How many endpoints each EPG may contain","A subject holds one or more filters, and each filter lists the traffic to match by protocol and port. Tenant ownership, bridge domain choice and endpoint limits are configured elsewhere.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:gnmi|topic:yang","An engineer sends a gNMI Set to an OpenConfig path on an NX-OS switch and wants a readable value in the request. Which encoding fits best?",,"JSON_IETF, which carries the value as IETF-style JSON","BYTES, which carries the value as an opaque binary blob","PROTO, which carries the value as a typed protobuf message only","ASCII, which carries the value as the CLI text","JSON_IETF is the human-readable encoding used with YANG-modelled data such as OpenConfig. BYTES and PROTO are not meant to be written by hand, and ASCII carries vendor text rather than YANG-modelled data.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops","How does a pull-based GitOps reconciler differ from a push-based pipeline?",,"A component inside the environment compares the repository with the live state and corrects differences on its own","A runner outside the environment pushes configuration when a person starts a job","It stores the live state in Git instead of the desired state","It requires every change to be made directly on the devices","In a pull-based model the reconciler runs next to the target, watches the repository and brings the target back to the declared state, which also corrects drift. A push-based pipeline acts only when it is triggered.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Which Jinja2 syntax removes the whitespace and the newline that precede a statement tag?",,"{%- ... %}","{%+ ... %}","{#- ... #}","{{! ... }}","A minus sign inside the opening delimiter strips the whitespace before the tag, and a minus before the closing delimiter strips it after. The plus form keeps whitespace, and the other forms are not whitespace control.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible","A task uses cisco.nxos.nxos_interfaces with state: replaced and sets only the description of Ethernet1/1. What happens?",,"The other attributes of Ethernet1/1 return to their defaults, and other interfaces stay unchanged","Only the description changes, and every other attribute of Ethernet1/1 is kept","Every interface not listed is reset to its defaults","The task fails, because replaced needs every attribute to be given","With state replaced, the listed interface is made to match the supplied attributes exactly, so unspecified attributes go to defaults, while interfaces that are not listed are left alone. Merged would keep other attributes, and overridden would reset unlisted interfaces.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|objective:cisco:350-901:1.2|topic:terraform","In Terraform, what is the purpose of a data source block?",,"It reads information about an object that already exists, without managing it","It creates a new object and records it in the state","It stores the Terraform state remotely","It defines the provider's credentials","A data source reads existing information, such as a fabric that another team created, so that other resources can refer to it. Resources create and manage objects, and backends and provider blocks have other roles.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:ansible|topic:ndfc|topic:troubleshooting","A long cisco.dcnm playbook runs for about 25 minutes. Early tasks succeed, and later tasks fail with 401 Unauthorized. What is the most likely cause?",,"The login token expired during the run","The playbook uses the wrong module names","The controller does not support the httpapi connection","The inventory lists the controller twice","Nexus Dashboard tokens are issued for a limited time, 20 minutes by default in the documented release, so a long run can outlive its token. Wrong module names would fail at the start, and an unsupported connection would never succeed.",4,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","What does default_operation='merge' do in an ncclient edit_config call?",,"It merges the supplied configuration into the existing configuration","It replaces the whole target datastore with the supplied configuration","It deletes the nodes that are named in the payload","It validates the payload without changing anything","The default operation tells the server how to treat nodes that carry no operation attribute, and merge combines the payload with what exists. Replace, delete and validate are different operations.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap|topic:day-0","A Nexus switch keeps restarting POAP discovery, and the DHCP pool has a lease of five minutes. What should the engineer change?",,"Set the lease to at least 3600 seconds","Remove option 67 from the pool","Move the TFTP server to another subnet","Add option 43 with the controller address","POAP needs a DHCP lease of at least 3600 seconds, so a short lease causes the process to fail and restart. Option 67 names the script, so removing it would break provisioning, and option 43 is not used by POAP.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:bash","Which NX-OS command runs one Linux command in Bash and then returns to the NX-OS CLI?",,"run bash ls /bootflash","bash enable ls /bootflash","python ls /bootflash","guestshell ls /bootflash","run bash followed by a command runs that command in the Bash shell and returns to the CLI, provided feature bash-shell is enabled. The python command starts the Python interpreter, and the other forms are not NX-OS syntax.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:ndfc|topic:nexus-dashboard","Which URL path prefix do REST calls to Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller use when they go through Nexus Dashboard?",,"/appcenter/cisco/ndfc/api/v1/","/restconf/data/","/ins/","/api/mo/","NDFC runs as a service on Nexus Dashboard and is reached under /appcenter/cisco/ndfc/api/v1/. RESTCONF, NX-API CLI and NX-API REST are served by the switches themselves.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Which endpoint does a client call to log in to NX-API REST and obtain a session cookie?",,"POST /api/aaaLogin.json","POST /ins/login","GET /restconf/login","POST /api/v1/infra/login","NX-API REST uses the same object model style as ACI, and the login is a POST to /api/aaaLogin.json with the user's name and password. NX-API CLI uses /ins, and the other paths are not NX-API login endpoints.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|topic:cml|topic:simulation","A simulated Nexus 9000v node is best suited to test which of these?",,"Configuration syntax and control-plane behavior of an automation change","Line-rate forwarding performance of the production fabric","The power consumption of a leaf switch","The physical cabling of the data center","A virtual Nexus runs NX-OS, so it exercises configuration and control-plane behavior. It does not reproduce hardware throughput, power draw or cabling.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","What is the main advantage of model-driven telemetry over polling a switch with SNMP?",,"The switch streams structured data on a schedule or on change, without a poll for every value","The switch answers each request faster because it uses UDP","The collector needs no knowledge of the data model","Telemetry replaces the need for any collector","Model-driven telemetry pushes structured, model-based data, which scales better than repeated polling. It does not rely on UDP, and the collector still needs to understand the data.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:telemetry|topic:grpc","What does sample-interval 60000 mean in an NX-OS telemetry subscription?",,"The data is sent every 60 seconds, because the unit is milliseconds","The data is sent every 60000 seconds","The subscription sends 60000 samples and then stops","The receiver waits 60000 milliseconds before connecting","The sample interval in an NX-OS subscription is in milliseconds, so 60000 means one sample per minute. It sets a period, not a sample count or a connection delay.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Which NX-OS show command does a script send through NX-API CLI to read CPU and memory usage?",,"show system resources","show interface brief","show ip route","show vlan","show system resources reports CPU and memory usage. The others report interfaces, routes and VLANs.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","A container in VLAN 120 reaches its gateway on the host but nothing beyond the leaf switch. A capture on the uplink shows untagged frames. What is the most likely cause?",,"The VLAN 120 subinterface or tagging on the host uplink is missing","The leaf switch has the wrong NX-OS version","The container's MTU is too large for the loopback interface","The veth pair has too many queues","Traffic for a tagged VLAN must leave the host with an 802.1Q tag, which a VLAN subinterface or a VLAN-aware bridge adds. Untagged frames on a trunk reach the native VLAN instead. The other options do not explain missing tags.",4,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:code-validation","An engineer wants an AI assistant to write a Python script that calls the NX-API REST interface. Which prompt practice most improves the result?",,"Include the relevant API documentation or schema and a sample of the expected output","Ask for the shortest possible script","Tell the model to be confident and skip comments","Remove the device type so that the answer stays generic","Giving the model the real API definition and an example grounds its answer and reduces invented endpoints. Brevity, confidence and generic prompts do not improve correctness.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|topic:mcp|topic:llm-agent","An MCP tool takes a switch name and returns interface counters. What should the tool definition include so that the model uses it correctly?",,"A clear description and a typed input schema for the arguments","The administrator password in the description","A list of every switch's running configuration","No description, so that the model has to guess how to use it","The model chooses and calls tools from their descriptions and schemas, so both need to be clear. Credentials and configurations do not belong in a tool definition, and a missing description leaves the model guessing.",2,2

multiselect[20]{tags,text,exhibit,c1,c2,c3,w1,w2,w3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.3|topic:dpu","Which two workloads are well suited to offload onto a DPU? (Choose two.)",,"Encryption and decryption of traffic, for example IPsec or TLS","Stateful firewalling and telemetry processing close to the workload",,"Running the full BGP best-path computation for the fabric","Storing the fabric's running configuration","Providing redundant power for the switch","A DPU takes infrastructure services such as encryption, stateful filtering and telemetry off the host CPU or switch ASIC. Fabric-wide control plane work, configuration storage and power supplies are not DPU functions.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Which two bridge domain settings are commonly used while VLANs are migrated into ACI in network-centric mode? (Choose two.)",,"L2 unknown unicast set to flood","ARP flooding enabled",,"A separate VRF for every VLAN","Contracts that deny all traffic between EPGs","Unicast routing enabled while the old gateway is still active","During migration the fabric is made to behave like the old Layer 2 network, so unknown unicast and ARP are flooded. Separate VRFs, deny contracts and a second active gateway would break the migrated servers.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|topic:yang|topic:openconfig","Which two statements about YANG models on NX-OS are correct? (Choose two.)",,"Native models such as Cisco-NX-OS-device cover the broadest set of NX-OS features","OpenConfig models need feature openconfig to be enabled on the switch",,"IETF models are the only ones that can carry operational state","Native models run unchanged on other vendors' equipment","OpenConfig models are always loaded and need no feature","Native models expose the whole NX-OS feature set but are specific to NX-OS. OpenConfig support is switched on with feature openconfig. Operational state is available in several model families, and native models are not portable.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops","Which two are advantages of a pull-based GitOps reconciler? (Choose two.)",,"Credentials for the environment stay inside it and are not stored in the CI system","Differences from the repository are corrected continuously",,"No repository is needed","Changes take effect only when a person starts a job","It cannot detect drift","A reconciler runs next to the target, so the CI system does not need credentials for it, and it keeps comparing the live state with the repository. It still depends on the repository and acts without a manual trigger.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Which two statements about Jinja2 are correct? (Choose two.)",,"Undefined variables render as empty text unless StrictUndefined is chosen","A base template can be extended with blocks so that each role overrides only what differs",,"The template runs on the switch when the configuration is applied","A for loop cannot be nested inside another for loop","Filters cannot be chained","Jinja2 is rendered on the control node, undefined variables are tolerated by default, and template inheritance with blocks supports shared structure. Loops can be nested and filters can be chained.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible|topic:aci","Which two statements about the cisco.aci Ansible modules are correct? (Choose two.)",,"They talk to the APIC rather than to individual switches","Most of them accept state present, absent and query",,"They connect to each leaf over SSH","They require Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller","They can only read data","The ACI modules call the APIC's REST API, and typical modules create, delete or query objects through the state parameter. They need neither SSH to leaf switches nor NDFC.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|objective:cisco:350-901:1.2|topic:terraform","Which two practices keep a secret out of Terraform source files? (Choose two.)",,"Pass the value through an environment variable such as TF_VAR_password","Read the secret from a secrets manager at run time",,"Commit a terraform.tfvars file that holds the password","Set the password as the default of the variable block","Print the password with an output so that it can be checked","Environment variables and secrets managers keep the value out of the repository. Files, defaults and outputs expose it in source control, in plans or in logs.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|objective:cisco:350-901:1.2|topic:terraform|topic:troubleshooting","Which two actions help to debug a Terraform provider error? (Choose two.)",,"Set TF_LOG=DEBUG to see the provider's API calls","Compare the provider version in use with the documentation for the argument that failed",,"Delete the state file before every run","Run apply repeatedly with -auto-approve until it succeeds","Remove the lock file so that provider versions float","Debug logging shows what the provider sent and received, and the documentation of the installed version shows which arguments exist. Deleting state, repeating applies and unpinning versions hide the problem or make it worse.",4,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Which two ncclient exceptions can a script catch to handle a failed login and a rejected request? (Choose two.)",,"ncclient.transport.errors.AuthenticationError","ncclient.operations.RPCError",,"ncclient.errors.GNMIError","ncclient.transport.errors.RESTCONFError","ncclient.operations.NXAPIError","ncclient raises AuthenticationError when the login fails and RPCError when the server returns an error for a request. The other names do not exist, because ncclient does not implement gNMI, RESTCONF or NX-API.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap|topic:day-0","Which two statements about a POAP script are correct? (Choose two.)",,"It is a Python script that runs on the switch","It can choose the image or configuration from details such as the serial number",,"It runs on the DHCP server","It needs Nexus Dashboard to run","It can only install an image that is already on the switch","The switch downloads the script and runs it, and the script decides what to fetch, often from the serial number or model. It downloads the image and configuration, and it does not depend on a controller.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:bash|topic:on-box","Which two statements about the Bash shell on NX-OS are correct? (Choose two.)",,"run bash sudo su opens a root shell when the user's role permits it","Files under /bootflash are reachable from the Bash shell",,"After feature bash-shell is enabled, the NX-OS CLI is no longer available","Bash commands bypass the role restrictions of the user","The Bash shell exists only in ACI mode","Bash is an additional shell beside the NX-OS CLI, it sees the switch's file systems, and it is still subject to roles. It is available in NX-OS mode after the feature is enabled.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|objective:cisco:300-635:3.5|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Which two are template types in Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller? (Choose two.)",,"POLICY","PROFILE",,"BACKUP","SCHEDULE","ROLLBACK","NDFC templates are of the type POLICY, which is applied to switches, or PROFILE, which is used for networks and VRFs. Backup, schedule and rollback are not template types.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Which two statements about NX-API CLI are correct? (Choose two.)",,"Show command output can be returned as structured JSON or XML","Configuration requests can be rolled back when a command fails",,"Only one command can be sent in each request","It returns only unformatted text","It needs SSH keys instead of HTTP credentials","NX-API CLI wraps CLI commands in HTTP requests, returns structured output and offers an error action for configuration. Several commands can be sent together, and authentication uses HTTP credentials.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Which two are benefits of testing an automation change on a simulated fabric? (Choose two.)",,"The fabric can be rebuilt identically for each pipeline run","Tests run without production hardware or risk",,"Simulated nodes reproduce the line-rate performance of production","No licenses or images are ever needed","Production monitoring becomes unnecessary","A simulation is repeatable and isolated from production. It does not reproduce hardware throughput, it can still need images and licenses, and it does not replace monitoring.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|topic:pyats|topic:genie","Which two statements about pyats learn are correct? (Choose two.)",,"It builds a structured model of a feature from several commands","The result can be saved to files and compared later with pyats diff",,"It changes the device configuration to match the model","It works on only one command at a time","It requires the device to run in ACI mode","learn collects the output of several commands and builds a feature model, and the saved snapshots can be compared. It only reads from the device and works on NX-OS mode devices.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Which two components are usually found downstream of a telemetry stream? (Choose two.)",,"A collector that accepts the stream","A time-series database or dashboard that stores and shows the data",,"A spanning tree root bridge","A DHCP relay agent","A POAP script","Streamed data goes to a collector, which stores it in a database for dashboards. Spanning tree, DHCP relay and POAP are unrelated to telemetry.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:2.6|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","Which two actions integrate NetBox with an automation workflow? (Choose two.)",,"Use the nb_inventory plugin so that Ansible builds its inventory from NetBox","Use a webhook so that a change in NetBox can start a pipeline",,"Copy NetBox's database file to each switch","Edit the switches directly and never update NetBox","Use NetBox only as a log server","NetBox provides an API that inventory plugins read and webhooks that trigger automation. Copying the database, bypassing the record or using it for logs misses its purpose.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Which two checks help to troubleshoot a bond interface on a Linux host? (Choose two.)",,"Read /proc/net/bonding/bond0 to see the mode and the state of each member","Check the matching port-channel or LACP configuration on the switch",,"Run ip route show to see bond membership","Run arp -a to see LACP state","Restart the container runtime","The bonding file shows the bond mode and the link state of each member, and the switch side must use a compatible configuration. Routes and ARP entries do not describe bond state.",4,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Which two practices reduce the risk that an AI agent misuses its access? (Choose two.)",,"Give the agent a read-only role for health queries","Require human approval before any change is applied",,"Share one administrator account among all agents","Hide the agent's actions from the logs","Let the agent approve its own changes","Least privilege and human approval limit what a misled agent can do. A shared administrator account, hidden actions and self-approval remove control and accountability.",4,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.4|topic:mcp|topic:llm-agent","Which two statements about the tools of an MCP server are correct? (Choose two.)",,"The model sees each tool's name, description and input schema","The application, not the model, executes the tool and returns the result",,"The model runs the tool itself on the switch","Tool descriptions are never sent to the model","A tool can run only if no schema is defined","The model decides which tool to call from its description and schema, and the application carries out the call. The model does not execute code, and schemas are what make calls well-formed.",2,2

match[20]{tags,text,exhibit,p1,r1,p2,r2,p3,r3,p4,r4,p5,r5,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:gnmi","Match each gNMI value encoding to its description.",,"JSON","Values encoded as plain JSON","JSON_IETF","Values encoded as JSON following the IETF YANG rules","PROTO","Values carried as typed protobuf messages","ASCII","Values carried as vendor text","BYTES","Values carried as an opaque binary blob","gNMI defines five encodings. JSON and JSON_IETF are readable, PROTO is typed binary, ASCII is text and BYTES is opaque.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|objective:cisco:300-435:1.5|topic:yang|topic:pyang","Match each YANG node type to its description.",,"container","Groups related nodes and holds no value of its own","list","Holds entries that are identified by a key","leaf","Holds a single value","leaf-list","Holds several values of the same type","rpc","An operation that a client can invoke","The node types decide how data is structured and addressed. A list needs a key, a leaf-list is an array of values, and an rpc is an operation, not data.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Match each ACI contract term to its meaning.",,"Provider","The EPG that offers the service","Consumer","The EPG that uses the service","Subject","A group of filters inside the contract","Filter","The protocols and ports to match","vzAny","All EPGs of a VRF treated as one group","A contract connects a provider and a consumer, and its subjects hold filters that match traffic. vzAny lets all EPGs of a VRF share one policy.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops","Match each GitOps term to its meaning.",,"Merge request","A proposal to change the main branch, open for review","Pipeline","The automated validation and deployment steps","Reconciliation","Bringing the live state back to the declared state","Branch protection","Rules that require review and passing checks before merge","Rollback by revert","Undoing a change with a new commit that reverses it","A merge request is reviewed, the pipeline automates checks and deployment, reconciliation corrects drift, branch protection enforces the rules, and a revert commit undoes a change without rewriting history.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Match each Jinja2 filter or expression to its effect.",,"vlans | join(',')","Joins the items into one comma-separated string","name | default('none')","Uses a fallback when the value is undefined","interfaces | length","Returns the number of items","name | upper","Converts the text to capital letters","interfaces | selectattr('enabled')","Keeps only the items whose enabled attribute is true","Filters transform values in a template: joining, defaulting, counting, changing case and selecting items by attribute.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.1|topic:ansible","Match each Ansible keyword to its use.",,"become","Run a task with elevated privileges","register","Save the result of a task in a variable","when","Run a task only if a condition is true","loop","Repeat a task for each item of a list","ansible-vault","Encrypt secret values in files","These keywords control privilege, results, conditions, repetition and secrets in playbooks.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|objective:cisco:350-901:1.2|topic:terraform","Match each Terraform command to its purpose.",,"terraform init","Downloads providers and prepares the working directory","terraform fmt","Rewrites files into the canonical style","terraform validate","Checks that the configuration is syntactically valid","terraform plan","Shows the changes that an apply would make","terraform destroy","Removes the managed objects","The commands cover preparation, formatting, validation, preview and removal of managed objects.",1,1
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|topic:troubleshooting","Match each error to its most likely cause.",,"terraform validate: Unsupported argument","The argument does not exist in the installed provider version","Ansible: the module cisco.nxos.nxos_vlans was not found","The collection is not installed, or the name is not fully qualified","Ansible: conditional check failed","The when expression evaluated to false for the registered data","Terraform: Cycle","Two resources depend on each other","Ansible: timeout waiting for the device","Connectivity problem, or a command timeout that is too short","Each message points to a typical cause: a mismatch with the provider version, a missing collection, a false condition, a circular dependency, or a connection or timeout problem.",4,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Match each NETCONF operation attribute to its effect.",,"merge","Combines the payload with the existing data","replace","Replaces the existing data with the payload","create","Adds the data and fails if it already exists","delete","Removes the data and fails if it does not exist","remove","Removes the data and succeeds if it does not exist","The operation attribute controls how a node is treated. Delete and remove differ in how they treat missing data, and create fails when the data exists.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Match each POAP item to its role.",,"DHCP option 67","Names the script file","DHCP option 150","Lists the TFTP server addresses","Script MD5 line","Lets the switch check the integrity of the script","Image .md5 file","Lets the script verify the downloaded image","DHCP lease of 3600 seconds or more","Required minimum so that POAP can complete","POAP depends on DHCP options for the script and the server, and on checksums for integrity. The lease must be long enough for the process to finish.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:python|topic:on-box","Match each NX-OS on-box Python item to its behavior.",,"cli()","Returns the command output as a string","clid()","Returns the output of a show command as JSON text","clip()","Prints the output and returns nothing","python","Starts the interpreter or runs a script from bootflash","source","Runs a Python script file from the CLI","The cli module has three functions that differ in what they return, and the python and source commands start scripts from the NX-OS CLI.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:ndfc|topic:nexus-dashboard","Match each Nexus Dashboard API item to its use.",,"POST /login","Obtains an authentication token","POST /refresh","Renews an existing token","/appcenter/cisco/ndfc/api/v1/lan-fabric/rest/control/fabrics","Lists the fabrics of NDFC","/appcenter/cisco/ndfc/api/v1/configtemplate/rest/config/templates/template","Creates a template","API key","Alternative to a username and password for scripts","Nexus Dashboard issues a token at login, which can be renewed, and NDFC resources are reached under its own path prefix. An API key is an alternative credential for scripts.",1,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Match each NX-API CLI request type to its use.",,"cli_show","Show commands with structured output","cli_show_ascii","Show commands with unformatted output","cli_conf","Configuration commands","bash","Linux commands in the Bash shell","rollback-on-error","Error action that undoes applied commands after a failure","The type field selects the kind of command, and the rollback option decides what happens when a configuration command fails.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:telemetry","Match each NX-OS telemetry configuration keyword to its role.",,"feature telemetry","Turns on dial-out telemetry","destination-group","Holds the receiver address, port, protocol and encoding","sensor-group","Holds the sensor paths","subscription","Ties sensor groups to destination groups","sample-interval","Period between samples, in milliseconds","These keywords build a dial-out subscription: the feature, the destinations, the data and the schedule.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Match each NX-OS show command to the health information it reports.",,"show system resources","CPU and memory usage","show interface counters errors","Interface error counters","show environment","Power supplies, fans and temperature","show module","State of line cards and supervisors","show processes cpu","CPU use by process","Each command reports a different part of device health, and a health script combines them.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Match each Linux command to what it shows.",,"bridge fdb show","The MAC addresses learned by the bridge","ip -d link show","Interface details, including VLAN IDs and the master device","tcpdump -e -nn -i eth0","Frames with link-layer headers, including VLAN tags","cat /proc/net/bonding/bond0","The mode and member state of a bond","ip netns exec ns1 ip addr","The addresses inside a network namespace","The commands expose the bridge table, interface details, VLAN tags, bond state and a namespace's own addresses.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:2.6|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","Match each source of truth item to its role.",,"NetBox","Records of IP addresses, VLANs, sites and devices","pynetbox","Python library for the NetBox API","nb_inventory","Ansible plugin that builds an inventory from NetBox","Webhook","Notification that can start a pipeline","Config context","Data attached to devices for rendering templates","NetBox holds the intended data, and the library, plugin, webhook and config context let automation read it and react to changes.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Match each part of a telemetry stack to its role.",,"gRPC","Transport used for dial-out streams","GPB","Binary encoding of the streamed data","Telegraf","Collector that receives the stream","InfluxDB","Time-series database","Grafana","Dashboards for the stored data","A common stack uses gRPC and GPB on the wire, Telegraf to receive, InfluxDB to store and Grafana to display.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.1|topic:ai|topic:llm","Match each AI term to its meaning.",,"Hallucination","The model states invented details with confidence","RAG","Retrieving documents and adding them to the prompt","Context window","The amount of text a model can consider at once","Temperature","Setting that controls how random the output is","Prompt injection","Input that tries to change the instructions the model follows","These terms describe common behaviors and settings of language models used for code and automation.",1,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|objective:cisco:300-435:5.4|objective:cisco:350-901:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.4|topic:mcp|topic:llm-agent","Match each part of an AI agent setup to its role.",,"LLM","Decides which tool to call and writes the answer","MCP server","Exposes tools, resources and prompts","MCP client","Connects the application to the server","Tool","An action that is invoked with arguments","Orchestrator","Application code that runs the loop and executes tool calls","The model chooses, the client and server carry the protocol, tools do the work, and the application orchestrates the loop.",1,2

order[20]{tags,text,exhibit,s1,s2,s3,s4,s5,s6,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|objective:cisco:300-435:1.2|topic:netconf","Place the events of a NETCONF session in the correct order.",,"The client opens an SSH connection and requests the netconf subsystem","Both sides send hello messages with their capabilities","The client sends an RPC such as get-config","The server returns an rpc-reply","The client sends close-session",,"A NETCONF session starts with the SSH subsystem and the capability exchange. RPCs and replies follow, and the session ends with close-session.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|objective:cisco:300-635:1.5|topic:gnmi","Place the steps of a safe gNMI configuration change in the correct order.",,"Send a Capabilities request to learn the supported models and encodings","Send a Get to read the current value","Send a Set with the update","Send a Get to confirm the new value",,,"Capabilities shows what the target supports, Get records the current value, Set applies the change, and a final Get confirms it.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Place the steps of moving an application from network-centric to application-centric mode in the correct order.",,"Map the VLANs one to one into bridge domains and EPGs with permit-any behavior","Move the Layer 3 gateway into ACI","Create the application EPGs","Move the servers into the new EPGs","Apply the contracts between the EPGs","Remove the empty legacy EPGs","The legacy design is migrated first and left permissive. Application EPGs are created and populated, contracts are applied once the traffic is understood, and empty legacy objects are removed last.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops","Place the steps of a pull-based GitOps reconciliation cycle in the correct order.",,"The reconciler fetches the repository","It reads the live state of the environment","It compares the two states","It applies the changes that bring the environment to the declared state","It reports the result",,"The reconciler reads the desired and the live state, finds the difference, applies the fix and reports. The cycle repeats continuously.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Place the steps of testing a configuration template before it is used in the pipeline in the correct order.",,"Lint the template syntax","Render it with sample data","Compare the output with a stored expected result","Fix any difference","Commit the template and the test data",,"Syntax is checked first, then rendering with known data, and the output is compared with an expected result. The template is committed after it passes.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|objective:cisco:350-901:1.1|topic:ansible","Place the steps of protecting a secret with ansible-vault in the correct order.",,"Create a vault password file outside the repository","Put the secret in a variables file","Encrypt the file with ansible-vault encrypt","Reference the file in the playbook","Run the playbook with the vault password file",,"The secret is stored in a file and encrypted before it is committed, and the playbook needs the vault password at run time.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|objective:cisco:350-901:1.2|topic:terraform","Place the steps of adding a new resource to a Terraform configuration in the correct order.",,"Write the resource block","Run terraform fmt","Run terraform validate","Run terraform plan","Review the plan","Run terraform apply","The block is written, formatted and validated before a plan is produced. The plan is reviewed and only then applied.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|objective:cisco:350-901:1.2|topic:terraform|topic:troubleshooting","Place the steps of troubleshooting a failed Terraform apply in the correct order.",,"Read the first error message","Enable debug logging with TF_LOG","List the objects in the state with terraform state list","Compare them with what the controller shows","Fix the cause","Run plan again before applying","The first error is the best clue, debug logging shows the provider calls, and the state is compared with the controller. After the fix, a new plan confirms what will change.",4,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:2.2|topic:ncclient","Place the steps of a careful configuration change with ncclient in the correct order.",,"Connect to the switch","Read the current configuration with get_config","Send the change with edit_config","Read the configuration again","Compare it with the expected result","Close the session","The current state is read before the change and compared afterwards, and the session is closed at the end.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Place the steps of preparing a modified POAP script in the correct order.",,"Edit the script","Make a copy of the script without the #md5sum line","Calculate the MD5 of that copy","Write the value into the #md5sum line of the script","Place the script on the TFTP server","Point DHCP option 67 at the script","The checksum is calculated over the script without its own checksum line, then inserted into the script before it is published and referenced by DHCP.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|topic:bash","Place the steps of running a Bash script on an NX-OS switch in the correct order.",,"Enable feature bash-shell","Open Bash with run bash","Create the script under /bootflash","Make it executable","Run it","Review the output","The shell must be enabled and opened before a script can be created, made executable and run.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.4|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Place the steps of using a template in Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller in the correct order.",,"Select the template","Create a policy with values for its variables","Attach the policy to the switches","Preview the pending configuration","Deploy it to the switches",,"A policy is created from a template, attached to switches, previewed, and deployed.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Place the steps of reading a managed object with NX-API REST in the correct order.",,"Enable feature nxapi","POST to /api/aaaLogin.json to get a session cookie","GET /api/mo/sys.json with the cookie","Read the imdata list of the reply",,,"The service is enabled, a login provides the cookie, the managed object is requested, and the data is read from imdata.",2,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:2.4|topic:cml|topic:simulation","Place the steps of building a digital twin of a fabric for testing in the correct order.",,"Export the topology and inventory from the source of truth","Build the CML topology file","Import the topology and start the lab","Apply the configurations","Run the validation tests",,"The twin is built from authoritative data, started, configured and tested.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.2|objective:cisco:350-901:3.4|objective:cisco:300-435:4.1|topic:pyats","Place the steps of running a pyATS job in the correct order.",,"Write the testbed file","Write the test script","Run pyats run job with the testbed","Read the results","Archive the results",,"The testbed and the tests are prepared, the job runs, and the results are read and kept.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Place the stages of the data path of a Telegraf-based telemetry stack in the correct order.",,"The switch collects the data of the sensor paths","The switch encodes the data as GPB","The switch sends it over gRPC dial-out","Telegraf receives it","InfluxDB stores it","Grafana displays it","The switch collects, encodes and sends the data. The collector receives it, and the database and dashboard store and show it.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Place the steps of enabling gNMI dial-in on a switch in the correct order.",,"Enable feature grpc","Set the grpc port","Assign the certificate trustpoint","Allow the default VRF with grpc use-vrf","Test with gnmic capabilities",,"The feature is enabled, the service is configured, and a test with a client confirms that it works.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nexus-dashboard","Place the steps of a health-monitoring script in the correct order.",,"Log in and keep the token","Collect the metrics","Compare them with thresholds","Create an alert for values over the limit","Send the alert to the team",,"The script authenticates, gathers data, compares it with limits and notifies the team when needed.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.2|objective:cisco:300-435:5.3|objective:cisco:350-901:4.2|topic:ai|topic:ai-security","Place the steps of introducing an AI agent for network operations safely in the correct order.",,"Define what the agent may do","Create a read-only account for it","Test it in a lab","Add human approval for any write","Enable it for a small group","Review its logs and widen access gradually","Scope and least privilege come first, followed by testing and approval for writes. Rollout starts small and grows while the logs are reviewed.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|objective:cisco:300-435:5.2|objective:cisco:350-901:4.5|topic:ai|topic:code-validation","Place the steps of checking an AI-suggested configuration in the correct order.",,"Read the suggested commands","Compare them with the platform documentation or the YANG model","Test them in a lab or simulation","Verify the result with automated checks","Apply them to production through the pipeline",,"The suggestion is checked against authoritative sources, tested and verified before it is deployed.",4,2

slotfill[20]{tags,text,exhibit,a1,a2,a3,a4,a5,d1,d2,d3,explanation,bloom,difficulty}:
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Fill in each blank so that gnmic streams interface counters every 10 seconds.","```bash\ngnmic -a 192.0.2.11:50051 -u admin -p 'C1sco123' --skip-verify subscribe --path /interfaces/interface/state/counters --stream-mode ⟦1⟧ --sample-interval ⟦2⟧\n```","sample","10s",,,,"on-change","target-defined","10","The sample stream mode sends values at a fixed interval, and the interval is written with a unit, here 10s. on-change sends only changes, target-defined leaves the choice to the device, and 10 has no unit.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.1|topic:openconfig|topic:gnmi","Fill in each blank to enable the gNMI service and the OpenConfig models on a Nexus switch.","```text\nswitch(config)# feature ⟦1⟧\nswitch(config)# feature ⟦2⟧\n```","grpc","openconfig",,,,"telemetry","nxapi","netconf","feature grpc starts the agent that serves gNMI, and feature openconfig enables the OpenConfig models. telemetry is for dial-out, nxapi for HTTP APIs and netconf for NETCONF.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:1.2|topic:aci","Fill in each blank with the ACI class that creates the object: a VRF, a bridge domain and an EPG.","```json\n{\n  \"fvTenant\": {\n    \"attributes\": {\"name\": \"Prod\"},\n    \"children\": [\n      {\"⟦1⟧\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"main\"}}},\n      {\"⟦2⟧\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"web-bd\"},\n                \"children\": [{\"fvRsCtx\": {\"attributes\": {\"tnFvCtxName\": \"main\"}}}]}},\n      {\"fvAp\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"shop\"},\n               \"children\": [{\"⟦3⟧\": {\"attributes\": {\"name\": \"web\"}}}]}}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```","fvCtx","fvBD","fvAEPg",,,"fvSubnet","vzBrCP","fvRsBd","fvCtx is the VRF, fvBD is the bridge domain and fvAEPg is the EPG inside an application profile. fvSubnet is a subnet, vzBrCP is a contract, and fvRsBd is the relation from an EPG to its bridge domain.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.1|objective:cisco:350-901:2.3|topic:gitops|topic:gitlab-ci","Fill in each blank so that the deployment job runs only for the main branch, and only when files of the fabric directory changed.","```yaml\ndeploy-fabric:\n  stage: deploy\n  script:\n    - ansible-playbook site.yml\n  rules:\n    - if: '$CI_COMMIT_BRANCH == \"⟦1⟧\"'\n      ⟦2⟧:\n        - fabric/**/*\n```","main","changes",,,,"merge","only","paths","A rules entry combines an if expression on the branch with a changes list of file patterns. only and paths are not rule keys here, and merge is not the name of the branch.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.2|objective:cisco:300-435:3.3|topic:jinja2","Fill in each blank with the filter that joins the VLAN IDs, supplies a fallback name, and counts the interfaces.","```jinja\nVLANs: {{ vlans | map(attribute='id') | ⟦1⟧(', ') }}\nHostname: {{ name | ⟦2⟧('unnamed') }}\nInterfaces: {{ interfaces | ⟦3⟧ }}\n```","join","default","length",,,"upper","sort","first","join builds one string from the items, default supplies a value when the variable is undefined, and length counts items. upper, sort and first do not do these things.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.3|topic:ansible","Fill in each blank with the state that matches the comment of each task.","```yaml\n- name: Add or update VLAN 10 only\n  cisco.nxos.nxos_vlans:\n    config:\n      - vlan_id: 10\n        name: WEB\n    state: ⟦1⟧\n- name: Read the VLANs from the device\n  cisco.nxos.nxos_vlans:\n    state: ⟦2⟧\n  register: current\n- name: Turn saved configuration text into structured data\n  cisco.nxos.nxos_vlans:\n    running_config: \"{{ saved_config }}\"\n    state: ⟦3⟧\n```","merged","gathered","parsed",,,"overridden","rendered","deleted","merged adds or updates the listed VLANs, gathered reads the current configuration from the device, and parsed converts supplied text into structured data. overridden would remove other VLANs, rendered builds commands without connecting, and deleted removes configuration.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.4|topic:terraform|topic:aci","Fill in each blank so that the VRF refers to the tenant, using the provider that manages an APIC.","```hcl\nterraform {\n  required_providers {\n    aci = {\n      source = \"⟦1⟧\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aci_tenant\" \"prod\" {\n  name = \"Prod\"\n}\n\nresource \"aci_vrf\" \"main\" {\n  tenant_dn = aci_tenant.prod.⟦2⟧\n  name      = \"main\"\n}\n```","CiscoDevNet/aci","id",,,,"CiscoDevNet/ndfc","dn","name","The ACI provider is published as CiscoDevNet/aci, and the id of an ACI resource is its distinguished name, which child objects use as their parent. ndfc targets another controller, and name is only the short name.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:2.5|objective:cisco:350-901:1.1|topic:ansible|topic:troubleshooting","Fill in each blank to run the playbook for one host with detailed connection debugging, and to print the whole inventory as JSON.","```bash\nansible-playbook site.yml ⟦1⟧ --limit leaf1\nansible-inventory --⟦2⟧\n```","-vvv","list",,,,"-v","graph","host","-vvv shows connection details, and --list prints the whole inventory as JSON. -v shows much less, --graph prints a tree, and --host shows the variables of one host.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.1|topic:ncclient|topic:netconf","Fill in each blank so that the script applies a change over NETCONF and reports a request that the switch rejects.","```python\nfrom ncclient import manager\nfrom ncclient.operations import ⟦1⟧\n\ndef apply_change(host, config):\n    # Purpose: apply one change over NETCONF and report a rejected request\n    with manager.connect(host=host, port=830, username='admin', password='C1sco123',\n                         hostkey_verify=False, device_params={'name': 'nexus'}) as m:\n        try:\n            m.⟦2⟧(target='running', config=config)\n        except ⟦3⟧ as err:\n            print(err.message)\n```","RPCError","edit_config","RPCError",,,"AuthenticationError","get_config","TimeoutExpiredError","RPCError is raised when the server rejects a request, and edit_config sends a change to the running datastore. get_config only reads, and AuthenticationError would be raised when the login fails.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.2|topic:poap","Fill in each blank with the names that carry the integrity information of a POAP script and of the image.","```text\n#!/bin/env python\n#⟦1⟧=\"b2c1d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8f9012\"\n\nn9000-dk9.10.4.3.F.bin.⟦2⟧\n```","md5sum","md5",,,,"sha256","checksum","hash","The POAP script carries an md5sum line in its header, and each downloaded file has a companion file with the extension .md5. The other names are not used by POAP.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.3|objective:cisco:300-435:2.7|topic:python|topic:on-box","Fill in each blank with the cli module function that returns the version text, returns the interfaces as JSON, and prints the clock.","```python\nfrom cli import *\nimport json\n\ndef report():\n    # Purpose: return the version text and the interfaces as data, and print the clock\n    text = ⟦1⟧('show version')\n    data = json.loads(⟦2⟧('show interface brief'))\n    ⟦3⟧('show clock')\n    return text, data\n```","cli","clid","clip",,,"run","exec","show","cli returns the output as a string, clid returns JSON text that json.loads can read, and clip prints the output. run, exec and show are not functions of the cli module.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.5|topic:ndfc|topic:templates","Fill in each blank so that the request creates a template in Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller.","```python\nimport requests\n\ndef create_template(host, token, body):\n    # Purpose: create a policy template in Nexus Dashboard Fabric Controller\n    url = f'https://{host}/appcenter/cisco/⟦1⟧/api/v1/⟦2⟧/rest/config/templates/template'\n    r = requests.post(url, json=body, headers={'Cookie': f'⟦3⟧={token}'}, verify=False)\n    return r.status_code\n```","ndfc","configtemplate","AuthCookie",,,"dcnm","templates","Authorization","NDFC is served under appcenter/cisco/ndfc, the template service is configtemplate, and the token from the login is sent in the AuthCookie cookie. dcnm is the old product name, and the other names are not in the path or header.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:3.6|topic:nxapi","Fill in each blank so that the script logs in to NX-API REST and returns the system managed object.","```python\nimport requests\n\ndef get_system(host):\n    # Purpose: read the system managed object through NX-API REST\n    s = requests.Session()\n    s.post(f'https://{host}/api/⟦1⟧.json', json={'aaaUser': {'attributes': {'name': 'admin', 'pwd': 'C1sco123'}}}, verify=False)\n    r = s.get(f'https://{host}/api/mo/⟦2⟧.json', verify=False)\n    return r.json()['⟦3⟧']\n```","aaaLogin","sys","imdata",,,"login","ins","result","The login is a POST to /api/aaaLogin.json, the system object is /api/mo/sys.json, and the reply carries its objects in imdata. /ins belongs to NX-API CLI.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.3|objective:cisco:350-901:3.1|objective:cisco:300-435:4.5|topic:telemetry|topic:mdt","Fill in each blank so that Telegraf receives gRPC dial-out telemetry from the switches on port 57000.","```toml\n[[inputs.⟦1⟧]]\n  transport = \"⟦2⟧\"\n  service_address = \":⟦3⟧\"\n```","cisco_telemetry_mdt","grpc","57000",,,"snmp","http","830","The cisco_telemetry_mdt input plugin receives dial-out streams, grpc is the transport, and the listening port here is 57000. snmp is a polling input, http is not a transport of this plugin, and 830 is the NETCONF port.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.4|topic:gnmi|topic:grpc","Fill in each blank with the commands that show the gRPC configuration and the statistics of the gNMI service.","```text\nswitch# show run ⟦1⟧\nswitch# show grpc ⟦2⟧ service statistics\n```","grpc","gnmi",,,,"telemetry","nxapi","netconf","show run grpc shows the gRPC configuration, and show grpc gnmi service statistics shows the counters of the gNMI service. The other words are different features.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.6|topic:python|topic:nxapi","Fill in each blank so that the function sends show system resources through NX-API CLI and returns the body of the output.","```python\nimport requests\n\ndef system_resources(host):\n    # Purpose: return the show system resources body from one switch\n    payload = {'ins_api': {'version': '1.0', 'type': '⟦1⟧', 'chunk': '0', 'sid': '1',\n                           'input': '⟦2⟧', 'output_format': 'json'}}\n    r = requests.post(f'https://{host}/ins', json=payload, auth=('admin', 'C1sco123'), verify=False)\n    return r.json()['ins_api']['outputs']['output']['⟦3⟧']\n```","cli_show","show system resources","body",,,"cli_conf","show interface brief","code","A show command uses the cli_show type, the input holds the command text, and the output of the command is in the body field. cli_conf is for configuration, another command would return other data, and code is the status field.",3,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.7|topic:linux|topic:containers","Fill in each blank to create a network namespace, move one end of a veth pair into it, and assign an address inside it.","```bash\nip ⟦1⟧ add ns1\nip link set veth-c0 ⟦2⟧ ns1\nip netns ⟦3⟧ ns1 ip addr add 10.1.0.2/24 dev veth-c0\n```","netns","netns","exec",,,"namespace","run","bridge","ip netns add creates a namespace, ip link set with netns moves an interface into it, and ip netns exec runs a command inside it. namespace, run and bridge are not subcommands for these jobs.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:4.5|objective:cisco:350-901:2.6|topic:source-of-truth|topic:netbox","Fill in each blank so that the webhook handler starts the pipeline for the device whose name is in the NetBox event.","```python\n@app.post('/netbox-webhook')\ndef hook():\n    # Purpose: start the pipeline when NetBox reports a changed device\n    event = request.get_json()\n    if event['⟦1⟧'] == 'updated' and event['model'] == 'device':\n        trigger_pipeline(event['data']['⟦2⟧'])\n    return '', 204\n```","event","name",,,,"action","id","type","A NetBox webhook payload holds the kind of event in event, the object type in model, and the object's data in data, where name is the device name. action and type are not the field names, and id would be the numeric identifier.",3,3
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.1|topic:ai|topic:llm","Fill in each blank with the message roles so that the instructions and the schema are given to the model correctly.","```python\nmessages = [\n    {'role': '⟦1⟧', 'content': 'You write NX-API REST scripts. Use only the schema that follows.'},\n    {'role': '⟦2⟧', 'content': f'Schema:\\n{schema}\\n\\nTask: list all VLANs.'},\n]\n```","system","user",,,,"assistant","tool","function","The system message sets the model's behavior, and the user message carries the task and the schema. The assistant role holds the model's own replies, and tool and function roles carry results of tool calls.",2,2
  "objective:cisco:300-635:5.3|topic:mcp|topic:llm-agent","Fill in each blank so that the function is exposed as an action for the model, has a typed argument, and the server talks over standard streams.","```python\nfrom fastmcp import FastMCP\n\nmcp = FastMCP('nexus-health')\n\n@mcp.⟦1⟧()\ndef cpu_idle(switch: ⟦2⟧) -> str:\n    # Purpose: return the CPU idle figure of one switch\n    return fetch_cpu(switch)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    mcp.run(transport='⟦3⟧')\n```","tool","str","stdio",,,"resource","int","http","The tool decorator exposes an action, the type hint str describes the switch name that goes into the input schema, and stdio makes the server communicate over standard streams. resource is read-only context, int is the wrong type for a name, and http is a network transport.",2,2
